{"questions":[{"question_id":"1lfxe40o2","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 2 Offline","year":2008,"examDate":2008,"subject":"physics","chapter":"electrostatics","chapterGroup":"electricity","topic":"electric-potential-energy-and-electric-potential","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pstatement-1--for-practical-purposes-the-earth-is-used-a-jee-advanced-physics-motion-468tqvubpfhwxal0","content":"<p>STATEMENT 1 : For practical purposes, the earth is used as a reference at zero potential in electrical circuits.</p>\n<p>and</p>\n<p>STATEMENT 2 : The electrical potential of a sphere of radius R with charge Q uniformly distributed on the surface is given by <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -1.045ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"5.37ex\" height=\"3.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -975 2373.6 1437\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(907.1,477.2) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D444\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D444\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(1073,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D700\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D700\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(499,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1975.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D445\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D445\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"2133.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Statement 1 is True, Statement 2 is True; Statement 2 is a CORRECT explanation for Statement 1"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Statement 1 is True, Statement 2 is True; Statement 2 is a NOT CORRECT explanation for Statement 1"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Statement 1 is True, Statement 2 is False"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Statement 1 is False, Statement 2 is True"}],"correct_options":["B"],"explanation":"<p>Statement 1 is True.</p>\n<p>The earth is used as a reference\nwith zero potential. The reasons are :\n<br><br>(i) Due to large size of the earth, its potential does\nnot change even if a small amount of charge is\ngiven to the earth or taken away from it. Also, all\nconductors on the earth which are not given any\nexternal charge, are very nearly at the potential\nV<sub>e</sub>. The choice of reference is quite arbitrary and\nis largely governed by convenience.\n<br><br>(ii) The earth is a good conductor. It is easily accessible for electrical circuits geographically distributed over it and hence it is used as a common\nreference with zero potentil.</p>\n<p>Statement 2 is true.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1lgmqyni3/485c357b-5fed-4de5-b2c0-b92559ec8f29/c354fbc0-de2b-11ed-b148-8b01c4181132/file-1lgmqyni4.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1lgmqyni3/485c357b-5fed-4de5-b2c0-b92559ec8f29/c354fbc0-de2b-11ed-b148-8b01c4181132/file-1lgmqyni4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Electrostatics Question 17 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1lgmqyni3/485c357b-5fed-4de5-b2c0-b92559ec8f29/c354fbc0-de2b-11ed-b148-8b01c4181132/file-1lgmqyni4.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1lgmqyni3/485c357b-5fed-4de5-b2c0-b92559ec8f29/c354fbc0-de2b-11ed-b148-8b01c4181132/file-1lgmqyni4.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1lgmqyni3/485c357b-5fed-4de5-b2c0-b92559ec8f29/c354fbc0-de2b-11ed-b148-8b01c4181132/file-1lgmqyni4.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1lgmqyni3/485c357b-5fed-4de5-b2c0-b92559ec8f29/c354fbc0-de2b-11ed-b148-8b01c4181132/file-1lgmqyni4.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1lgmqyni3/485c357b-5fed-4de5-b2c0-b92559ec8f29/c354fbc0-de2b-11ed-b148-8b01c4181132/file-1lgmqyni4.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1lgmqyni3/485c357b-5fed-4de5-b2c0-b92559ec8f29/c354fbc0-de2b-11ed-b148-8b01c4181132/file-1lgmqyni4.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>V = <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -1.045ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"5.37ex\" height=\"3.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -975 2373.6 1437\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(907.1,477.2) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D444\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D444\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(1073,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D700\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D700\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(499,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1975.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D445\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D445\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"2133.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>Therefore, statement 2 is correct explanation for statement 1.</p>"}]}